🚀 Day 22 of #DrGViswanathanChallenge

Today, I solved LeetCode 78 – Subsets.

Today’s problem was a great introduction to Backtracking / Recursion. The main idea was to generate every possible subset by making a choice for each element: include it or exclude it.

💡 Approach: Recursion + Backtracking

For every element, I explored two possibilities:

✅ Include the current element in the subset.
❌ Exclude the current element and move ahead.

When i == nums.size(), I reached the end of the array, so the current subset was added to the answer.

The push_back() and pop_back() operations helped me maintain and restore the current subset while exploring different possibilities.

📚 What I Learned:

✅ How recursion can be used to explore multiple choices.
✅ Understanding the include/exclude pattern.
✅ Basics of backtracking using push_back() and pop_back().
✅ How a recursion tree generates all possible combinations.
✅ Understanding why n elements produce 2ⁿ subsets.

⏱️ Time Complexity: O(n × 2ⁿ)
💾 Space Complexity: O(n) auxiliary recursion space (excluding the output)

